refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;

 intmemory_get_peak_usage
 boolreal_usage&false;



 Returns the peak of memory, in bytes, that's been allocated to your PHP
 script.

&reftitle.parameters;
real_usage
Set this to &true; to get the total amount of memory that PHP's memory manager has reserved from the system, including pages that are not currently in use. It is not the amount of memory the operating system has given to the PHP process, which is typically much larger. If not set or &false; only the memory used by emalloc() is reported.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns the memory peak in bytes.
When PHP's memory manager is disabled by setting the USE_ZEND_ALLOC environment variable to 0, this function always returns 0, whatever the value of real_usage.
